{"name":"Angora Goat","hex":"#ede7de","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"angora goat","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of angora (“type of goat”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/angora_goat"}],"entries":[{"title":"Angora goat","blocks":[{"text":"The Angora or Ankara is a Turkish breed of domesticated goat. It produces the lustrous fibre known as mohair. It is widespread in many countries of the world. Many breeds derive from it, among them the Indian Mohair, the Soviet Mohair, the Angora-Don of the Russian Federation and the Pygora in the United States."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Angora_002.jpg/330px-Angora_002.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Angora_goat"},{"title":"Goat","blocks":[{"text":"The goat or domestic goat is a species of goat-antelope that is mostly kept as livestock. It was domesticated from the wild goat of Southwest Asia and Eastern Europe. The goat is a member of the family Bovidae and is closely related to the sheep. It was one of the first animals to be domesticated, in Iran around 10,000 years ago."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Hausziege_04.jpg/330px-Hausziege_04.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goat"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Mohair_goats-nanny_with_newborn._-_DPLA_-_f92a422df737028204114eb061497348.jpg/500px-Mohair_goats-nanny_with_newborn._-_DPLA_-_f92a422df737028204114eb061497348.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Mohair_goats-nanny_with_newborn._-_DPLA_-_f92a422df737028204114eb061497348.jpg/500px-Mohair_goats-nanny_with_newborn._-_DPLA_-_f92a422df737028204114eb061497348.jpg?utm_source=en.wikip